&lt;h2&gt;


The Coors Field trap
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Look at who is on the lucky list: a Rockie. Then sort pitchers by ERA minus xERA (120+ innings): Colorado's Kyle Freeland has a 6.65 ERA against a 5.54 xERA, one of the biggest "unlucky" gaps in baseball.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is not luck. &lt;strong&gt;xwOBA and xERA ignore the ballpark.&lt;/strong&gt; Coors Field's thin air turns fly balls into hits and home runs, so Rockies hitters will always look lucky and Rockies pitchers unlucky. Before you call a regression, check where the player plays half his games.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Who hits the ball hardest
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Barrel rate, 400+ PA: Munetaka Murakami 20.5% (35 HR), James Wood 18.6% (30), Nick Kurtz 18.0%, Shohei Ohtani 16.2%, Mike Trout 16.0%.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Is a gap meaningful?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Across 205 hitters with 400+ PA, the gap has a standard deviation of about 19 points, and a third of hitters are more than 20 points off. A gap of 40+ is unusual, and park effects and sprint speed explain part of it. Chandler Simpson (.305 wOBA, .263 xwOBA, zero home runs) is the textbook case: xwOBA barely credits speed, and he beats out ground balls it scores as outs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Data and a ready-made scraper
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The joined 2026 table (1,619 hitters and pitchers, season stats plus Statcast) is free on Kaggle: &lt;a href="https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/kenmutisya/mlb-stats-statcast-sample" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MLB 2026 Player Stats with Statcast&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you'd rather not maintain the join, I put it on Apify as &lt;a href="https://apify.com/scrapemint/mlb-stats-statcast" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MLB Stats &amp;amp; Statcast&lt;/a&gt;. It does the season leaderboard, lookups by player name, and games with probable pitchers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Witt bounce-back or not?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Transfermarkt's market values are the closest thing football has to a price index. Agents quote them, clubs argue with them, and fantasy and betting models use them as a cheap proxy for squad strength.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I pulled every player in the &lt;strong&gt;Premier League, LaLiga, Serie A, Bundesliga and Ligue 1&lt;/strong&gt; (2,623 players, €35.6 billion in total) to see what the numbers say. First, how to get them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The endpoints
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Transfermarkt's own front end talks to a JSON service. No key, and it takes batches:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight http"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="na"&gt;GET https://tmapi-alpha.transfermarkt.technology/players?ids[]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;418560&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ids&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;433177&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="no"&gt;GET&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;https&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;//tmapi-alpha.transfermarkt.technology/club/281/squad&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;GET https://tmapi-alpha.transfermarkt.technology/clubs?ids[]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;281&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ids&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;11&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The player record has &lt;code&gt;marketValueDetails.current&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;.previous&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;.highest&lt;/code&gt; (value in EUR plus the date), &lt;code&gt;attributes.contractUntil&lt;/code&gt;, position, foot and height, and &lt;code&gt;clubAssignments&lt;/code&gt; with the current club and national team. Value history and transfer fees come from two more endpoints on the main site:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight http"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="no"&gt;GET&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;https&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;//www.transfermarkt.com/ceapi/marketValueDevelopment/graph/418560&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="no"&gt;GET&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;https&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;//www.transfermarkt.com/ceapi/transferHistory/list/418560&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Batches of 25 ids work fine, so a whole league (20 squads, about 550 players) takes around 45 requests.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ids&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'418560'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'433177'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'937958'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'https://tmapi-alpha.transfermarkt.technology/players?'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ids&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`ids[]=${i}`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;join&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;'&amp;amp;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;url&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'User-Agent'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'Mozilla/5.0'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mv&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;marketValueDetails&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;current&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;log&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;lifeDates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;age&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sb"&gt;`€${mv.value / 1e6}M`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s1"&gt;'contract to'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;attributes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;contractUntil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Erling Haaland 26 €220M contract to 2034-06-30&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Bukayo Saka 25 €110M contract to 2030-06-30&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Lamine Yamal 19 €220M contract to 2031-06-30&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


1. Value peaks at 24 and halves by 28
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Median market value by age, all 2,623 players:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Age&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Median value&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Players&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;19&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;€5.0M&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;121&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;21&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;€8.0M&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;181&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;23&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;€8.5M&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;234&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;24&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;€12.0M&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;224&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;25&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;€12.0M&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;198&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;26&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;€9.0M&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;225&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;28&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;€6.0M&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;179&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;30&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;€5.0M&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;107&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;32&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;€3.0M&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;86&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The curve peaks at 24 to 25 and drops by half within three years. Some of that is resale value: at 28 a club is buying a player's peak years, not an asset it can sell on. Some is survivorship: the 32-year-olds still in a top-5 league are a selected group, and their values are still low.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. The richest squads
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Club&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Squad value&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Manchester City&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;€1.50B&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Real Madrid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;€1.50B&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Arsenal&lt;/td&gt;
