&lt;h2&gt;


⚛️ React
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 &lt;a href="https://github.com/Pagepro/nexity" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Nexity - Next.js + Sanity with AI workflows built in. 16 skills, 9 agents, project-specific rules and read-only code reviewers. MIT.&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🐦 &lt;a href="https://x.com/rickyfm/status/2125593907048091950" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Ricky Hanlon leaves Meta after 8 years on React&lt;/a&gt; - Most of the React core team has already left Meta. He will keep working on React at a new company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔐 &lt;a href="https://github.com/remix-run/react-router/security" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Router vulnerabilities - 4 high and 3 moderate advisories, upgrade to 7.18.6 or 8.5.2&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔐 &lt;a href="https://opensourcemalware.com/blog/react2steal-github-actions" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React2STEAL - Automated campaign exploits unpatched React and Next.js servers from hijacked GitHub accounts&lt;/a&gt; - At least 1,281 servers still vulnerable to React2Shell (React 19.0–19.2) or to the Next.js middleware bypass were hit, and their env vars, &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt; files and API keys were committed to public GitHub repos. If you're still on a vulnerable version, upgrade and rotate your secrets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👀 &lt;a href="https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/101695" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Next.js PR - Switchyard, an experimental Go server in front of &lt;code&gt;next start&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; - For now, it only forwards requests to Node. Routing could move to it over time, and requests to the experimental &lt;a href="https://levelupgo.dev/blog/nextjs-go-route-handlers" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Go Route Handlers&lt;/a&gt; would skip Node entirely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💬 &lt;a href="https://github.com/TanStack/query/discussions/12669" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TanStack Query v6 roadmap&lt;/a&gt; - Planning a small major with few breaking changes. ESM-only, React 19 minimum to use &lt;code&gt;use()&lt;/code&gt; for Suspense, scheduler using microtasks, deprecated APIs removed, stable &lt;code&gt;streamedQuery&lt;/code&gt;. Considering the removal of &lt;code&gt;enabled&lt;/code&gt; in favor of &lt;code&gt;skipToken&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://sigh.dev/posts/vibecoding-faster-react-tests/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Testing Library is faster when it's part of the DOM&lt;/a&gt; - What if a DOM implementation had built-in Testing Library queries? &lt;code&gt;@ctrl/dom&lt;/code&gt; replaces &lt;code&gt;jsdom&lt;/code&gt; for component tests and runs existing RTL test suites 32–54% faster. Node 26+ and React 19 only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://www.zachleat.com/web/npm-audit-report/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Your Tools are Hiding npm Audits from You&lt;/a&gt; - A fresh Next.js app reports 0 vulnerabilities. But its 139 dependencies bundled in &lt;code&gt;next/dist/compiled&lt;/code&gt; have 3 critical and 19 high ones, which &lt;code&gt;npm audit&lt;/code&gt; can't see.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://www.gmoniava.com/blog/react-forms-beyond-onsubmit" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React Forms Beyond onSubmit&lt;/a&gt; - Compares &lt;code&gt;onSubmit&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;onSubmit&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;useTransition&lt;/code&gt;, and the &lt;code&gt;action&lt;/code&gt; prop on a newsletter subscription form, with a summary table.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://pierre.computer/writing/on-drawing-icons" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;On Drawing Icons&lt;/a&gt; - The Figma-to-React pipeline behind Pierre icons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 &lt;a href="http://joyofreact.com/?couponCode=TWIR" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;The Joy of React - Build an intuition for how React really works through an interactive learning experience. On sale for Black Friday!&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://diffs.com/words" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Pierre Words - Streaming Markdown renderer written in WebAssembly, with a React renderer&lt;/a&gt; - Built for streamed AI replies. Its own benchmark against Streamdown highlights 6x less streaming work, 20x less memory, and a 65% smaller React renderer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://github.com/lxsmnsyc/talata/releases/tag/talata%400.4.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Talata 0.4 - Drop-in faster replacement for remark - Now parses MDX&lt;/a&gt; - It claims to parse MDX 4x faster than &lt;code&gt;remark-mdx&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📦 &lt;a href="https://github.com/reduxjs/redux-toolkit/releases/tag/v2.15.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Redux Toolkit 2.15 - Per-store RTK Query runtime, &lt;code&gt;initiate()&lt;/code&gt; promises resolve with their own result, function &lt;code&gt;pollingInterval&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;startReason&lt;/code&gt;, readable type hovers&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
