&lt;h2&gt;


📱 React-Native
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ffmkqkio3f5oqq0yld46v.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Ffmkqkio3f5oqq0yld46v.jpg" alt="Reanimated 4.8" width="800" height="314"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://swmansion.com/blog/shared-element-transitions-in-reanimated-4-8-0/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reanimated 4.8 - Shared Element Transitions stable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One of the most anticipated features is finally stable, and enabled by default! Tag two views with the same &lt;code&gt;sharedTransitionTag&lt;/code&gt;, put them in two &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;SharedTransitionBoundary&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; components, and when the target boundary becomes active, the view travels to it. Think of an album cover moving from a song list into the now-playing screen. It's a small detail, but it makes transitions feel much more natural.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Transitions are no longer tied to navigation, so they also work between tabs, or between two views on the same screen. The moving view is the actual view, not a snapshot, so its content keeps running during the transition. On iOS, it even follows your finger during a swipe-back gesture. When the two views have different children, the new &lt;code&gt;SharedTransition.fadeContent()&lt;/code&gt; modifier fades them out and in.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Other key highlights include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Animated text&lt;/strong&gt; - Support for &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;Animated.Text&amp;gt;{sharedValue}&amp;lt;/Animated.Text&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. The UI thread updates text without any React re-render.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CSS animations&lt;/strong&gt; - CSS animations and transitions interpolate &lt;code&gt;backgroundImage&lt;/code&gt; gradients, and can animate &lt;code&gt;borderCurve&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;writingDirection&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;verticalAlign&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;objectFit&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Lighter animations&lt;/strong&gt; - Cutting a lot of unnecessary work from every frame.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;a href="https://github.com/software-mansion/react-native-reanimated/releases/tag/worklets-0.14.0" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Worklets 0.14&lt;/strong&gt; - WebSocket on Worklet Runtimes, abortable runtimes, &lt;code&gt;runOnRNSync&lt;/code&gt; from other runtimes, new docs with a visual Learn section&lt;/a&gt; - Supports React Native 0.87 → 0.89, pairs with Reanimated 4.8.x&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




